mira_cs: FYI — onboarding ramp for Orbitly is hitting intermittent 429s during SDK init. They followed the starter-kit and spawn a bunch of preflight calls from the browser. Trying to avoid blocking their ramp tomorrow. Account: orb-8732. Logs below. :eyes:

mira_cs: ```
[2026-03-22T15:02:14Z] preflight POST /v1/sessions -> 429
Response headers: x-ratelimit-window: 60, x-ratelimit-remaining: 0
curl -i -H "Authorization: Bearer <ephemeral>" "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/sessions"
```

oliver_eng: Do they use browser SPA per-tab ephemeral tokens? That pattern often causes thundering preflight. Quick checks: are they reusing connections (keep-alive / single WebSocket) or creating a new fetch per tab? Also check ephemeral token TTL vs concurrency.

sam_devex: Two immediate mitigations we can give them: (1) gate preflight with a local mutex so only one request per tab does the heavy handshake, (2) exponential backoff + jitter on 429s. Example JS pattern:```
const MAX_CONC = 4;
const sleep = (ms) => new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms));
async function retryWithJitter(fn, retries=5){
  for(let i=0;i<retries;i++){
    try { return await fn(); }
    catch(e){
      if(e.status !== 429) throw e;
      const jitter = Math.random()*1000;
      await sleep((2**i)*250 + jitter);
    }
  }
  throw new Error('failed after retries');
}
```

irina_support: Adding: please confirm whether this is the browser SDK vs server-side. Browser + one-ephemeral-per-tab is most common. Also send me their desired ramp cadence (reqs/s) so we can check account quota windows; if needed we can open a temporary quota bump.

mira_cs: Confirmed: browser SPA, QA spawns 8 tabs simultaneously during load tests. They mint ephemeral tokens per tab. Ramp target is ~180 req/min during onboarding tests.

oliver_eng: Ok — 180/min across 8 tabs = bursty windows. For short term: ask them to (A) consolidate token issuance (1 token per session), (B) stagger tab starts by ~250–500ms, (C) reuse keep-alive connection where possible. I can also whitelist orb-8732 for a short window so onboarding won't be blocked.

ratebot: quota-change: temporary quota grant +30% applied to orb-8732 until 2026-03-24T12:00:00Z by support ops.

sam_devex: Sharing a tiny client snippet they can drop into starter-kit to coalesce preflight and limit concurrent preflight attempts:```
class Semaphore{ constructor(n){ this.n=n; this.waiters=[] }
 async acquire(){ if(this.n>0){ this.n--; return }
  await new Promise(r=>this.waiters.push(r));
}
 release(){ this.n++; if(this.waiters.length) this.waiters.shift()(); }
}
const PRE_SEM = new Semaphore(1);
async function preflightOnce(fn){ await PRE_SEM.acquire(); try{ return await fn(); } finally{ PRE_SEM.release(); } }
```

mira_cs: Perfect — I'll send the above snippets + the short checklist to Orbitly and schedule a 30m sync. Thanks all. :thumbsup:

oliver_eng: If they still see 429s after client changes, ping me and I'll run a quick traffic trace and adjust policy rules.

irina_support: Logged: CASE-9982 for orb-8732, assigned to support ops; recording the temporary quota bump and onboarding call time.

mira_cs: Appreciate the fast help — passing to Orbitly now.
